/target
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json
secrets/
id_rsa*
findings.md
progress.md
task_plan.md

# `core.ignorecase=true` (macOS) makes `progress.md` above also match
# `PROGRESS.md`, which v4 tracks as the build log. Re-include it explicitly.
!/PROGRESS.md

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Go
/agent/bin/
/ztpd/bin/
*.o
/agent/bpf/vmlinux.h
/agent/bpf/devbox_*_bpfeb.go

# bpf2go output is tracked, one pair per architecture.
#
# A CO-RE object can only be produced on a Linux host of the target
# architecture with BTF, so leaving it untracked meant a source build on macOS
# had no way to embed the eBPF agent and silently fell back to proc polling.
# Committing the generated pair is the cilium/ebpf convention. These negations
# must come after `*.o` above, which would otherwise swallow the objects.
!/agent/bpf/devbox_*_bpfel.go
!/agent/bpf/devbox_*_bpfel.o

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
/labkit/dist/
/labkit/*.egg-info/

# Browser-automation scratch output. Written into the repo root by the
# Playwright MCP server during manual verification; never part of a build.
.playwright-mcp/
